# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
config RUST_X86_COMPRESSED
	bool "Rust x86-64 gzip extraction and KASLR implementation"
	depends on RUST && X86_64 && KERNEL_GZIP && CC_IS_CLANG
	help
	  Build the compressed kernel's extraction, gzip decoder, KASLR,
	  command-line parsing and error reporting in a freestanding Rust crate.
	  Its core library is rebuilt for the early-boot small-model PIE ABI;
	  the already-decompressed kernel's Rust runtime is never linked here.

	  The retained C files are the reference implementation. Other boot,
	  EFI, startup, memory-encryption, page-table, CPU-feature and console objects still
	  have C production owners and are explicit migration gaps. This option
	  does not establish that the whole boot image is implemented in Rust.
